{
  "description": "Kanhe protocol objects added in specification revision v0.2, built by an independent Python encoder from spec/kanhe.cddl: a passkey and hardware key registration (actor-set-presence), statements with proof of presence (an Ed25519 WebAuthn assertion; a hardware key's signature over the challenge), a delegation that requires presence, the state commitment (root, proofs, and the log entry that carries it), and a cosign request. The record's type is a user's, example.document/1, with the generic lifecycle (regenerated in v0.9, which removed the built-in industry types). All signatures are Ed25519 (deterministic), so every object must be reproduced byte for byte. Keys are throwaway test keys: seed = SHA-256(\"Kanhe test key: <name>\").",
